Build CAPYDORO, a pomodoro timer app in a single HTML file with an onsen (hot spring) theme.

**Core timer**: Large circular countdown (MM:SS) in center with work/break/long-break phases cycling continuously. Default durations: Focus = 25 min, Soak = 5 min, Deep Soak = 15 min. Display phase label ("Focus", "Soak", "Deep Soak"), cycle number (Pomodoro #1, etc.). Auto-start next session when current one ends.

**Visual design**: Circular SVG progress ring that drains as time counts down. Warm onsen palette as default theme: dark brown background (#2a1f18), warm orange work phase (#f0a35e), muted green break phase (#8fc9a8), cream text (#f5e8d7). Animated steam wisps rising above the timer (3 staggered strokes with blur, floating upward continuously). Responsive, centered layout with monospace numbers.

**Controls**: Start/Pause button (shows "Start"/"Resume"/"Pause"), Skip, Reset. Space key toggles start/pause. Update document title to show current time and phase.

**Settings panel** (gear icon, top-left): Editable numeric inputs for Focus, Soak, Deep Soak durations (1–120 min each), and pomodoros-per-deep-soak count (1–12). Checkbox "Tick last 10 sec" plays a soft high-frequency tick sound during final 10 seconds of any phase. All settings persist to localStorage with validation.

**Theme picker** (color dot + "Theme" button, top-right): Eight themes—Onsen (default, warm), Classic, Tokyo Night, Ocean, Forest, Rose, Ember, Light—each with distinct CSS custom properties. Persist theme choice to localStorage.

**Audio**: Generate Web Audio API chimes via sine oscillators—three rising notes (C5 E5 G5) for work-done, two-note callback (E5 C5) for break-done. Each note has soft attack, long decay, and quiet octave-up partial for shimmer. Optional triangle-wave ticking at final 10 seconds when enabled.

**Daily yuzu counter**: Display "N yuzu earned today" with yellow/brown SVG yuzu icon below controls. Persist per-day using localStorage with date key; auto-reset at midnight. Increment count when a Focus session completes.

**UX**: Use `Date.now()` timestamp-based timing to survive tab throttling; update display ~4 times per second. Settings/theme panels close when clicking outside or pressing Escape. Show hint below counter: "A chime plays when each session ends. Space = start/pause." Responsive, centered layout.
